Keep your response concise — this is a checkpoint, not a full session summary.

### Output Format (IMPORTANT)
Record durable learnings using the XML blocks below so they persist to memory.
Only include a block if you have something concrete to store; omit empty blocks.

- Put updates about the *user* (communication style, preferences, workflows,
  frustrations) inside a `<user_updates>` block. Start each entry with a
  Markdown section header (e.g. `## Communication Style`) so it merges into
  the matching section of USER.md.
- Put cross-cutting *session* learnings (decisions, reusable patterns, facts)
  inside a `<session_memory>` block as bullet points; these append to MEMORY.md.

Example:
<user_updates>
## Communication Style
- Prefers concise bullet points over prose
</user_updates>

<session_memory>
- Tests are run with `pytest -x` for fast feedback
- The MCP middleware is skipped entirely when no servers are configured
</session_memory>
